vsm1.7:59.1:
Similarly, he can also be called “blessed” (bhagavā) when he can be called “possessed of abolishment” (bhaggavā)
owing to the following menaces having been abolished; for he has abolished (abhañji) all the hundred thousand
kinds of trouble, anxiety and defilement classed as greed, as hate, as delusion, and as misdirected attention;
as consciencelessness and shamelessness, as anger and enmity, as contempt and domineering, as envy and avarice, as deceit and fraud,
as obduracy and presumption, as pride and haughtiness, as vanity and negligence, as craving and ignorance;
